      </div>

      <div class="faq-grid">
        <div class="faq-item active">
          <div class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
            <span>How are NG Global agency service charges structured?</span>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-icon-arrow"></i>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            NG Global operates with transparent, government-compliant service charges. We do not demand unaccounted advance deposits. Once you register, our career executive coordinates 1-on-1 on WhatsApp to evaluate your trade credentials and explain the exact milestone-based fee structure before you commit. In addition, we regularly offer 100% Company-Sponsored Quotas where overseas employers cover all agency expenses for selected trades.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <div class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
            <span>Why are some international jobs completely free with zero service charges?</span>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-icon-arrow"></i>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            A select few international positions have zero service charges because overseas principal companies fully sponsor the recruitment and hiring costs directly to us for those specific project quotas. In these specific cases, candidates do not pay any service charges.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <div class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
            <span>How do official visa application and processing payments work?</span>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-icon-arrow"></i>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            Candidates pay all official visa application fees, GAMCA medical examinations, and consular biometric processing charges directly to the relevant foreign embassies, government portals, or authorized diagnostic clinics. You never pay government visa fees to personal accounts of unverified agents.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <div class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
